+What not to report: style, formatting, naming, missing comments or docs, the wording of docs, comments or messages (unless it is code, a command or a number people will copy or act on, and it is wrong), alternative designs, costs nobody would notice (an import, an allocation, one extra call), missing logs or metrics, bookkeeping a tool fixes (go.mod "indirect" markers, lock files), and anything about code outside the changed lines unless the change breaks it. Never praise. If the hunks hold no defect, return an empty findings list. Use severity "nit" only for a small, clearly useful fix, and never more than one or two.
 
